@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "osb.zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Partner Ticket Integration
	Testing user ticket updates in Zendesk caused by partner changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner1                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner1                          |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner2                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner2                          |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.partner3                      |
	| Email Address | osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                               |
	| Last Name     | Partner3                          |
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Manager" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Member" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I assign a user the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker with the role "Watcher" to the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page	

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the partner workers with the following email addresses for the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	* I wait for "5" seconds
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken |
	| osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View ticket after partner requester removal on organization with partner workers
	Zendesk tickets should be reassigned if a partner requester is removed from OSB.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I remove a user the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker from the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I remove a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker from the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	And I get the email address of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I attempt to remove a user the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker from the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner" who still has an open Zendesk ticket
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken"

Scenario: View ticket after partner requester removal on organization with partner watcher
	Zendesk tickets should be reassigned if a partner requester is removed from OSB and a watcher is present.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name                       | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code                       | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type                       | Group              |
	| Industry                   | Automotive         |
	| Partner Code               | Zen OSB Partner    |
	| Partner First Line Support | true               |
	| Tier                       | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts               | 10                 |
	| Address Line               | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country                    | United States      |
	| State                      | California         |
	| City                       | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip                        | 91765              |
	| Region                     | US                 |
	| Language                   | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner3@lrpartner.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	And the user with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" should be in the organization "Zen OSB Automotive"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I create a request as a user with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" with the following values
	| Product           | prd_liferay_portal_6_2                           |
	| Component         | activation_key_project_administration            |
	| System Status     | production_functioning_with_limited_capabilities |
	| Subject           | Request Subject                                  |
	| Description       | Request Description                              |
	| Organization Name | Zen OSB Automotive                               |
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I remove a user the email address "osb.partner1@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker from the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner"
	And I get the email address of the default user belonging to the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" from zendesk.liferay.com
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken"
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I attempt to remove a user the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken" as a worker from the partner with the code "Zen OSB Partner" who still has an open Zendesk ticket
	Then the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the status "new"
	And the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the requester with the email address "osb.partner2@lrpartner.com.broken"